  "result": "I'm wrapping up the archive search. The closest past report is a pinned path fallback not appearing on the dock.\n\n{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#46587\"], \"answer\": \"This looks like a known limitation, not a fix on your side. When you type a path such as c:\\\\ into Command Palette, the result is a fallback item, and fallback items can't be pinned to the Dock. PowerToys#46587 describes the same behavior: the Dock records the pin but nothing appears, and that ticket includes pinning full paths. A maintainer said fallbacks generally shouldn't be pinnable, and that improvements for path pinning were already in progress. Until that ships, keep using your mapped-drive entry, which works. You can also try updating to the latest PowerToys release to see whether the improvement is included. If c:\\\\ still can't be pinned after updating, add your PowerToys version and logs to that ticket. I only found one ticket on this, and it doesn't mention drive roots specifically, so I can't be sure it is exactly the same problem.\"}",
